      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Deviation (recorded): this page is filed under gu-houses because Yue Yang Palace is a named Immortal Gu House. It is mobile equipment of Heavenly Lotus Sect, not a five-region map seat.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Shi Zheng Yi lists Canary Pavilion, Yue Yang Palace, and Heavenly Pool when asking whether Heavenly Lotus Sect has a fourth Immortal Gu House.",
      "chapters": [
        1233
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "sect-house-listing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_shi_zheng_yi"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At Emperor City, the palace at the left is grand and imposing. Together with Frost Dragon Manor it charges Bai Ning Bing and the rest, and destroys their house’s killer move. Fang Yuan treats his house as not their match and orders a retreat. With Wind Sweeping Building restraining that house, Yue Yang Palace moves rapidly like a meteor and crashes into it.",
      "chapters": [
        1708
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "emperor-city-combat",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
